  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "ART-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The Hilbert norm group fixes the direction of the Artin map",
      "anchor": "inputs-artin-norm",
      "statement": "For a number field K with Hilbert class field H, the idèle-class norm N_(H/K)(C_H) is the image in C_K of the idèles that are units at every finite place. The induced map α_K:G_K→Cl(𝒪_K) is onto and locally constant. It kills inertia and takes a lift of arithmetic Frobenius at 𝔭 to [𝔭], so α_K(D_𝔭)=⟨[𝔭]⟩.",
      "hypotheses": "Choose an algebraic closure of K. H is the ray class field of the unit modulus with empty real support. 𝔭 is any finite prime and a prolongation is chosen.",
      "definitions": [
        "C_K=𝔸_K^×/K^×. An idèle is in the standard open subgroup exactly when its component and inverse component are integral at each finite place.",
        "Art_K:Cl(𝒪_K)≃Gal(H/K) takes an ideal prime to its arithmetic Frobenius. On the absolute group α_K=Art_K⁻¹∘res_H.",
        "The modulus-one ideal ray group is the ordinary ideal class group. All real signs occur in the standard subgroup."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-artin-norm-equation"
      ],
